      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GOD'S CROSS (1) comes through a handy trial at Lark Hill recently after ending his previous campaign in Saturday grade. He comes right back in grade first-up and he shapes as a progressive type on resumption. Can lob into a midfield position and run over the top of his rivals late. COSMIC GEM (2) finished off strongly from midfield to finish 0.7L off the winner. He was in the market there and should be fitter for that run. He maps beautifully and with the added fitness on his side, he can raise the bar again now. EIGHTYSEVEN LAD (3) got the job done narrowly last start as a $1.75 fave at Kalgoorlie. This is tougher, but he was showing promising signs prior to that and now Pike hops in the irons. Can sit handy and be tough to run down. EXTRONIZE (5) surprised last start at this track and trip, but he can prove she's not a one hit wonder. ELLOVAMAN (9) won't be far away.",
